;; clj-kondo configuration for vaelii-foreign.
;;
;; `with-cleared-kb` (vaelii.foreign.test-util) binds a KB symbol the way `let`
;; does — `(with-cleared-kb [kb tu/fresh] …)` — and clj-kondo can't see a binding a
;; macro introduces, so without this every `kb` inside one reads as an `Unresolved
;; symbol`. `:lint-as` teaches it the let shape; the matching `:unresolved-symbol`
;; exclude carries the uses `:lint-as` alone doesn't reach. Core's own config gives
;; its wider set of KB binding macros the same treatment.
;;
;; `[clojure.test :refer :all]` is the one blessed refer-all (matches vaelii
;; core's convention); exempt it so the test namespaces don't trip the
;; refer-all linter.
{:lint-as
 {vaelii.foreign.test-util/with-cleared-kb clojure.core/let}

 :linters
 {:unresolved-symbol
  {:exclude [(vaelii.foreign.test-util/with-cleared-kb)]}

  :refer-all {:exclude [clojure.test]}}}
